      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Ah, working with high-density racking in Rotterdam, I see! It's quite the challenge, but with the right approach, you'll have those stacks standing tall and sturdy as a well-built fortress. When it comes to the center of gravity, think of it like a tightrope walker balancing on a thin wire – you want to keep that center of gravity as low as possible to avoid tipping over. So, make sure your heavy items are placed at the bottom, and lighter ones on top. As for interlocking patterns, it's like a game of chess with your goods – each piece must be in the right spot to keep the whole structure stable. Try using a pattern that distributes weight evenly, like a checkerboard, so that no single point bears too much pressure. And remember, always double-check your work, because even the smallest oversight can lead to a domino effect of disaster. Keep those warehouse goblins at bay with your meticulous planning and careful execution!",
